LIMITATIONS
No browser, alternative UI surface, or visual QA was used because browser access was explicitly denied.
Scaffold compilation or checkpoint tests do not mean the full learner projects are complete. Existing foundation, systems, and service evidence is reused without claiming new execution.
cargo audit compares lockfiles with the fetched RustSec database; it is not a source-code audit, vulnerability-free guarantee, license audit, or independent review.
Final audits use unfiltered targets and no ignored advisories. Warnings do not fail default cargo-audit exit status; the unmaintained warning is reported explicitly.
Build/test commands use explicit outer-cache target directories. cargo audit and cargo tree have no target-dir build option and do not compile artifacts.
No dependency manifests or existing native/UI dependency versions were edited. Cargo generated the UI scaffold initial lockfile while resolving its declared versions.
Sandboxed advisory fetch and UI scaffold registry access initially failed; approved retries completed. Final outputs are in their named logs.
The no_std library was tested on the host; no claim is made about board support, interrupts, MMIO, or an embedded executable.
